edit("Table IV compares", whole="Table IV compares encoder and predictor combinations trained under identical conditions. The proposed GIN + GRU reaches 70.2% accuracy and 0.906 AUROC on guided edits, against 59.1% and 0.718 for GCN + GRU, 64.1% and 0.855 for GraphConv + GRU, and 69.5% and 0.901 for GIN + LSTM. GIN + GRU gives the highest guided-edit AUROC, followed closely by GIN + LSTM, which supports the choice of GIN as the graph encoder. All models give ASD detection AUROC values near the chance level of 0.5, and random edits stay near 0.5 for every model.")
